<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="GBrowser: Install" id="GBrowser-Installation">

    <primary-label ref="gbrowser"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Install: <ui-path>Settings | Plugins | Marketplace</ui-path>, search for GBrowser</p>
        <p>Requires: JetBrains IDE 2026.3 (build 263.3889 or a later 263 build)</p>
        <p>License: free and open source (Apache-2.0)</p>
    </tldr>

    <link-summary>Check the requirements, install GBrowser from JetBrains Marketplace or from disk, and open the tool window.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>Check the requirements and install GBrowser from JetBrains Marketplace.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>Install the free GBrowser plugin in IntelliJ IDEA and other JetBrains IDEs from JetBrains Marketplace or from disk, and check the requirements.</web-summary>

    <p>
        GBrowser is a plugin for JetBrains IDEs that adds the <control>GBrowser</control> tool window, an embedded Chromium browser.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Requirements" id="requirements">
        <list>
            <li>
                The current version, 2026.3.1, works with JetBrains IDEs 2026.3: builds 263.3889 to 263.*, which includes the 2026.3 EAP.
                It does not install on later IDE versions.
                For JetBrains IDEs 2026.2, JetBrains Marketplace offers GBrowser 2026.2.3.
            </li>
            <li>
                The IDE must run on a runtime with JCEF support, such as the bundled JetBrains Runtime.
            </li>
            <li>
                The bundled <control>Web Browser (JCEF)</control> plugin must be enabled.
                GBrowser depends on it and cannot be enabled without it.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Install GBrowser" id="install">
        <procedure title="Install from JetBrains Marketplace" id="install-from-marketplace">
            <step>
                Open the <control>Settings</control> dialog (<shortcut>Ctrl+Alt+S</shortcut>, macOS: <shortcut>⌘ ,</shortcut>)
                and select <control>Plugins</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Open the <control>Marketplace</control> tab.
            </step>
            <step>
                Type <code>GBrowser</code> in the search field.
            </step>
            <step>
                Click <control>Install</control> next to GBrowser.
            </step>
            <step>
                If the IDE asks you to restart, click <control>Restart IDE</control>.
            </step>
        </procedure>

        <procedure title="Install from disk" id="install-from-disk">
            <p>Use this method when the IDE has no access to JetBrains Marketplace.</p>
            <step>
                Download the plugin ZIP file that matches your IDE version from the
                <a href="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/14458-gbrowser/versions">GBrowser versions page</a>.
            </step>
            <step>
                In the <control>Settings</control> dialog, select <control>Plugins</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Click the gear icon and select <control>Install Plugin from Disk...</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                Select the downloaded ZIP file and click <control>OK</control>.
            </step>
            <step>
                If the IDE asks you to restart, click <control>Restart IDE</control>.
            </step>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Check the installation" id="verify">
        <p>
            After the installation, the <control>GBrowser</control> button appears on the left tool window bar.
            To open the browser and start browsing, see <a href="Work-with-GBrowser.topic" anchor="open-gbrowser"/>.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="License" id="license">
        <p>
            GBrowser is free and open source under the Apache-2.0 license.
            There is no trial and no license key.
            The source code is on <a href="https://github.com/edgafner/GBrowser">GitHub</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            To support development, use the <control>Support GBrowser and help keep it free</control> link at the top of the GBrowser settings page.
        </p>
    </chapter>

